speechtext:
I am surprised to observe . the difference in the salaries paid to various fishery officers in Nova Scotia. For instance, Mr. Aylmer, of Meteghan, gets a salary of $500, in addition to travelling allowance. Mr. Burke, of Albert Bridge,
138}
gets $165. Mr. J. M. Campbell, of Halifax, gets only $15. I see in the Auditor General's Report the name of another officer whose salary is $500, and another who receives as small an amount as $60.
